# Command: ID (Read and Answer frames)
# Radio: Kenwood TS-480HX / TS-480SAT
# Title (cover, verbatim): "PC CONTROL COMMAND REFERENCE FOR THE TS-480HX/ SAT
#   TRANSCEIVER"
# Printed revision: NONE printed; cover carries "KENWOOD CORPORATION",
#   "(c) 2003/11/28" and the printing code line "09 08 07 06 05 04 03 02 01 00".
# Source page: printed folio "10"  ==  PDF page 11 of 26
# Charts used: the Read and Answer charts of the ID block.  The block ALSO prints a
#   "Set" row whose ruler 1..10 is drawn and whose ten cells are ALL EMPTY - see
#   FINDING F3.  (The TS-590 book omits the Set row from its ID block entirely
#   rather than printing it empty.)
# Derivation date: 05/09/2026
# NO code, no generator, no other file and no other document was consulted.
#
# COUNTED FRAME LENGTHS (two independent counts of the printed numbered ruler, then a
# third look at 600 dpi to confirm the Set row really is blank and not faint):
#   ID Set    = 0 positions filled (ruler printed 1..10, every cell empty)
#   ID Read   = 3 positions
#   ID Answer = 6 positions
#
# CHARTS, position by position:
#   Set:     1..10 all empty
#   Read:    1 I  2 D  3 ;                          (4..10 empty)
#   Answer:  1 I  2 D  3 P1  4 P1  5 P1  6 ;        (7..10 empty)
#
# Field map:
#   pos 1-2  "ID"
#   pos 3-5  P1  (three characters)
#   pos 6    ";"
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ID LEGEND, VERBATIM (every model/number pair printed; the complete right-hand
# column; block description reads "Reads the transceiver ID number."):
#
#   Parameters:
#   P1
#     020: TS-480
#
#   ONE pair, and only one.  The book does NOT distinguish TS-480HX from TS-480SAT
#   here; both are "020: TS-480".  (The model split is carried by the TY command
#   instead - see TY-480.golden.)
#
# POSITIONS THE CHART PRINTS AS FIXED / "Always": NONE in the ID block.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BYTES WHOSE VALUE THE MANUAL DOES NOT DETERMINE  -> INHERITED-ASSUMED
#   NONE for the Read and Answer frames below: every byte is determined by the
#   printed chart and the printed legend.
#   No Set vector is emitted, because the Set chart is empty (FINDING F3) and
#   inventing one would be resolving that finding.
#
# Hardware status: UNVERIFIED for every vector in this file.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VECTORS  (name <TAB> frame bytes verbatim)
#
id480_read	ID;
id480_answer_ts480	ID020;
